content:
{
  "asset": "Pump P-111 — AquaDyne HF-300, serial HF3-21100; reported grinding noise from the non-drive-end bearing.",
  "priority": "P2",
  "stop_equipment_now": false,
  "condition_assessment": [
    {
      "statement": "Vibration: the applicable limits are the HF-300 Figure 3 bearing-housing vibration-velocity zones, with the highest reading from both housings used for classification. The reported 4.2 mm/s is above the 2.8 mm/s RMS Zone A/B boundary but below 4.5 mm/s RMS, placing it within Zone B (2.8–4.5 mm/s RMS, 'Long-term operation'). It does not reach Zone C at 4.5 mm/s RMS ('Restricted — plan maintenance') or Zone D at 7.1 mm/s RMS ('Damage likely — stop the pump'). Therefore, the SSP-07 immediate-stop rule for the manufacturer's highest severity zone is not triggered by this reading. Confirm that the reported value is RMS velocity measured on a bearing housing.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Temperature: the applicable decision limit is the manufacturer's bearing-temperature alarm limit; SSP-07 requires a priority-1 work order within the shift when that limit is exceeded. HF-300 temperatures are measured on the bearing-housing surface, but the supplied manual extract contains no numeric alarm limit. Consequently, 74 °C cannot be classified as below or above the alarm limit, and a P1 temperature trigger can neither be confirmed nor excluded. The provisional P2 priority must be escalated to P1 if 74 °C is found to exceed the manufacturer's alarm limit.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Bearing noise: manual section 5.3 applies directly—replace both bearings as a pair when either bearing shows wear, noise or high temperature. The reported non-drive-end grinding noise therefore requires bearing-pair replacement even though the vibration reading remains in Zone B.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Seal: the report says the seal is dry and does not report shaft-seal leakage. The troubleshooting action to replace the mechanical seal is listed for 'Leakage at shaft seal'; that row does not by itself justify seal replacement here. Do not interpret a dry exterior as evidence that the seal has run dry without clarification.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "probable_causes": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing wear or damage, most likely at the non-drive end, is the leading suspected cause because of the localised grinding noise. Bearing wear is also a listed cause of high vibration; inspect both bearings, but replace them as a pair on the noise criterion regardless of which one is defective.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Shaft misalignment is a listed cause of both high vibration and high bearing temperature. Check alignment; the temperature contribution remains conditional on establishing whether 74 °C is actually above the applicable temperature criterion.",
      "citations": [
        "C09",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Impeller imbalance or damage, or cavitation, are alternative listed causes of high vibration. Inspect the impeller and check NPSH rather than attributing all findings to the bearing without inspection.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Over-greasing is a listed cause of high bearing temperature and should be checked if the temperature is confirmed excessive. The evidence does not establish that 74 °C is excessive or provide the correct grease quantity.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "tasks": [
    {
      "statement": "Review the existing condition-monitoring records and confirm which bearing housing produced the 4.2 mm/s reading, whether it was RMS vibration velocity, and which housing or housings measured 74 °C. For ongoing monitoring, measure vibration velocity on both bearing housings weekly and classify the highest reading using Figure 3.",
      "citations": [
        "C01",
        "C06",
        "C07"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Before opening the pump, electrically isolate and apply LOTO at the MCC; mechanically isolate the suction and discharge valves; drain and vent the pump; and complete the required line-break permit.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Check grease quantity and alignment. Inspect the bearings and impeller for wear, damage or imbalance, and check NPSH for possible cavitation. Record the findings before corrective reassembly.",
      "citations": [
        "C09"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Replace both bearings as a pair under manual section 5.3 because the non-drive-end bearing is noisy: install one HF3-510 non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3 and one HF3-512 drive-end bearing 6312-C3.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Reassemble disturbed fasteners with lightly oiled threads to Table 5 as applicable: bearing-housing bolts M12 to 85 Nm; impeller nut M24 to 160 Nm if removed; casing bolts M16 to 210 Nm if disturbed; and seal-gland nuts M10 to 25 Nm if disturbed on this serial-number asset. Fit a new HF3-120 casing gasket whenever the casing is opened.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "After any work that moves the motor or bearing housing, perform laser shaft alignment. Acceptance tolerances are parallel offset 0.05 mm and angular misalignment 0.05 mm per 100 mm.",
      "citations": [
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Following return to service, resume weekly velocity measurements on both bearing housings and classify the highest result. If a reading enters Zone D, stop the pump immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C06",
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "parts": [
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-510",
      "description": "Non-drive-end bearing 6310-C3; replace as part of the required bearing pair.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-512",
      "description": "Drive-end bearing 6312-C3; replace together with the non-drive-end bearing.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C10"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_number": "HF3-120",
      "description": "Casing gasket; required if the casing is opened, because it must be replaced whenever the casing is opened.",
      "quantity": 1,
      "citations": [
        "C05"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "safety_controls": [
    {
      "statement": "SSP-07 Rev 3 applies to this pump. For work inside the pump or on its seal, use electrical isolation and LOTO at the MCC, mechanical isolation of suction and discharge valves, and a line-break permit with draining and venting completed first.",
      "citations": [
        "C14",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If any component to be lifted weighs more than 25 kg, obtain a lifting plan signed by the shift supervisor and use certified lifting equipment.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If P-111 is confirmed to be on a chemically dosed line, use chemical goggles and nitrile gloves. The explicit sodium-hypochlorite dosing note identifies only P-101 through P-106, so it does not establish P-111's chemical service.",
      "citations": [
        "C15",
        "C16"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "The present 4.2 mm/s reading is not in the manufacturer's highest severity zone. If any verified highest housing reading enters Zone D (7.1–11.0 mm/s RMS on the shown axis), stop the machine immediately and notify the reliability engineer before restart.",
      "citations": [
        "C07",
        "C15"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "If the manufacturer's bearing-temperature alarm limit is obtained and 74 °C exceeds it, raise or escalate the work order to P1 within the shift.",
      "citations": [
        "C15"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "labour": [
    {
      "statement": "Bearing replacement, pair: standard labour allowance 6.0 hours with 2 technicians.",
      "citations": [
        "C12"
      ]
    },
    {
      "statement": "Laser alignment: standard labour allowance 1.5 hours with 1 technician when required because the motor or bearing housing has been moved.",
      "citations": [
        "C10",
        "C12"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "source_conflicts": [
    {
      "statement": "Seal part and gland-torque conflict: the manual parts list specifies component seal HF3-450, and Table 5 specifies 25 Nm for M10 seal-gland nuts. SB-2026-014 instead specifies cartridge seal HF3-450B, 30 Nm gland torque and a 0.1 mm sleeve-scoring replacement criterion, but those instructions apply only to HF-300 pumps serial HF3-22000 and above. P-111 is serial HF3-21100, below that range, so the bulletin does not apply. If seal work is separately authorised, this asset continues to use HF3-450 and Table 5, including 25 Nm gland torque; do not substitute HF3-450B or apply the bulletin's 30 Nm instruction. The dry-seal report alone does not authorise seal replacement.",
      "citations": [
        "C05",
        "C09",
        "C11",
        "C13"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "open_questions": [
    "What is the manufacturer's numeric HF-300 bearing-housing temperature alarm limit, and which housing or housings measured 74 °C? The supplied evidence does not provide the limit needed to decide whether the P1 temperature rule applies. [C01, C15]",
    "Was the 4.2 mm/s reading RMS vibration velocity on a bearing housing, which housing was measured, and what was the reading on the other housing? The manual requires classification of the highest reading from both housings. [C06, C07]",
    "What are the weights of the back pull-out assembly and any other components to be lifted? No weights are supplied, so it is unknown whether the greater-than-25 kg lifting-plan control is triggered. [C15]",
    "Is P-111 on a chemically dosed line, and what is its process fluid? The only explicit chemical-dosing list covers P-101 through P-106, not P-111; chemical goggles and nitrile gloves are required if the line is chemically dosed. [C15, C16]",
    "Does 'seal is dry' mean no visible external leakage, or is there separate evidence that the seal has run dry? These conditions lead to different troubleshooting interpretations. [C09]",
    "What are the specified grease type and acceptable grease quantity, the NPSH acceptance criterion, and the full bearing disassembly/reassembly instructions? The supplied extract directs these checks but does not provide their detailed criteria; section 5.3 supplies only the pair-replacement rule. [C09, C10]",
    "Will the bearing-replacement disassembly open the casing or disturb the mechanical seal? Confirm this before work so that gasket and any separately justified seal scope can be finalised; a new casing gasket is mandatory if the casing is opened. [C05, C10]",
    "SSP-07 supplies a P1 trigger for excessive bearing temperature but no P2/P3 definitions in the provided evidence. Confirm the provisional P2 classification against the site's remaining priority rules, while escalating to P1 if the temperature alarm limit is exceeded. [C15]"
  ]
}
